Z||000000||David Bartlett||09-02-2001||02:30 AM||||Yea I know its a bandwagon thing but I like reading about them.<P>Anyone ever consider a Stealth/Mitsubishi 3000gt Twin Turbo? The stock six is a 3.0 DOHC. I figure that would make the turbos about the right size. Plus you would have the problem of spooling up.<P>The only reason I ask is that i have seen one in the scrap yard and wondering if I should grab the parts for another day.||||reg||1
Z||000001||artherd||09-02-2001||03:35 AM||||GRAB IT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Even if you have to rebuild them (which I recomend in any event) you can't beat junkyard prices.  Get everything you can off the car.<P>I think Twin Turbo Fieros aren't popular/haven't been done (I'm reluctant to say that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> simply because of space, and $, constraints making it 'hard enough' <BR>to do a single larger turbo.<P>The Mitsu makes 320bhp from that 3.0 litre turbo motor, sounds fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (I'd recomend a 3.4 or a de-stroked 3.4 (which would be I belive a 3.2 if memory serves) they have the 2.8's oiling problems fixed.)<P>Let us know how it goes!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by David Bartlett:<BR><B>Yea I know its a bandwagon thing but I like reading about them.<P>Anyone ever consider a Stealth/Mitsubishi 3000gt Twin Turbo? The stock six is a 3.0 DOHC. I figure that would make the turbos about the right size. Plus you would have the problem of spooling up.<P>The only reason I ask is that i have seen one in the scrap yard and wondering if I should grab the parts for another day.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||pontiacs4me||09-02-2001||04:03 AM||||Actually that engine makes 300 hp.  A friend of mine just bought a 93 Vr4 last thursday and we took it to the track tonight.  It turned a 15.06 at 93mph.  He still needs some launching lessons and he should be well into the 14's.  He pulled a 2.15 60 foot, then a friend of mine pulled a 2.02, but he only got it to run a 15.09.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||09-04-2001||02:01 AM||||Later cars got a 20hp bump.<P>And ran the 1/4mile in 14seconds at 100mph I belive.<P>Launch procedures for this car are simple.  Rev to 5-6k, drop clutch.<P>It should haul ass, those 60' times in particuliar are rather high. <P>Fun to see one light up all 4 tyres though.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B>Actually that engine makes 300 hp.  A friend of mine just bought a 93 Vr4 last thursday and we took it to the track tonight.  It turned a 15.06 at 93mph.  He still needs some launching lessons and he should be well into the 14's.  He pulled a 2.15 60 foot, then a friend of mine pulled a 2.02, but he only got it to run a 15.09.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||BlackDragon||09-04-2001||02:17 AM||||all 4 tires? are they all wheel drive or did i miss something?<P>------------------<BR>im looking for a inexpensive black standard fastback. does not have to run. does not have to look good. only the mid section needs to be dent free. the fenders,bumpers, dont have to be in good cond. faded paint is fine. anyone who has info, email me. grey interior would be nice but beggars cant be choosers||||reg||1
Z||000005||RedOktober||09-04-2001||02:55 AM||||Here is a copy of some guys dyno testing a TT set up vs a single Turbo setup.<BR> <BR>We set boost to (a conservative) 18 psi and let the dogs out. It should be noted that horsepower output was not a concern of this exercise. Our goal was to simply illustrate the boost curve. The assigned boost level was nowhere near the peak efficiency of either system and was far from the max pressure these cars run on the street. Furthermore, low-end and mid-range tuning could play a role in the power output of the engines (which would only cloud the picture in a small "quick tech" style article). However, this exercise has really whet our appetites and we plan to feature both cars in depth and do a no-holds-barred dyno comparison in a future issue. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tur0301a3_singlevstwin04.jpg"> <BR>Dyno Chart<BR>As expected, the twin set-up (red) delivered more boost at lower engine speeds and the single moved more air on the top. But the differences were not as pronounced as we expected. As for peak power? That's an issue we will address in a future, no-holds-barred article. Stay tuned. <P>And from personal experience, I switched the Twin turbo set up on an Gen III RX to a single Turbo set up. I found that there was a bit of lag, buy nothing the seat of the pants driving could feel. <P>On the Fiero's, the V6 produces enough low end torque, that a TT would not be needed.(Unless u really wanted it.) If I had a chance to play with both turbo's for cheap, I would be all over it. <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/red6[1]a.jpg">   <BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"<p>[This message has been edited by RedOktober (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||pontiacs4me||09-04-2001||03:27 AM||||<BR> <P>He tried to get the tires to spin, they wouldnt even spin the other night when it rained.  Maybe something is wrong with it.  I noticed that the boost guage reads about 13 psi maxed out, but everywhere ive read it says stock it puts out 9 psi.  We looked every where under the hood, and cant find a boost controller, so maybe the guage is off.  <BR>And from what ive read about the later models, is stock they pull a 14.7 at about 95 mph.  And as for 60 foots I think a 2.02 is really good for a car that weighs 4000 lbs, seings how my firebird ran 2.28 60's but manages mid 14's at 99-100 mph.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Kwez||09-04-2001||09:23 PM||||pontiacs4me-<BR>it might be chipped to raise the max boost ...<BR>but then I would expect it to be faster than a stock one ! ??<P>blackdragon-<BR>yep AWD !<BR>it's amazing the traction you get w. AWD + good tires, my Impreza accelerates just as fast (w. butt dyno anyways) on a wet road as on a dry road. <BR>(& that's a car that does a solid 5.5sec 0-60, maybe a bit faster)||||reg||1
Z||000008||88 Fiero||09-04-2001||11:00 PM||||Twin Turbo on a Fiero never been done before??? Acutally "IFG" did a twin turbo on a fiero back in the late 80's. The price was around $4,500.00. The set-up was very interesting but never got it right. Had a few people who bought it finding themselves rebuilding the engine. FOCOA has an article on this set-up||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||09-04-2001||11:03 PM||||Hrm, that is abnormal, even accounting for differences between tyres.<P>In (I belive) a '95 3000GT have laid 4 strips of rubber over 20feet long on dry pavement, slightly uphill infact.  It is a scary scary awesome feeling  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>A common gremlin in these cars (because of the incredible power coupled with AWD traction) is clutch-slip.  I would target that first.<P>There should be blowoffs/bypasses in the intake manifold itself somewhere, I've only ever just seen into the engine bays, and it's been a while  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The good news is, there's plenty of potential in that car, it ought to be running 14.5s or so. (the 320hp cars do 14.3s) at about 100mph.<P>60' times should be very low, like 1.8sec or so. (!!)  These are from memory, and like I said, it's been a while (late 1997  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>since I've had a chance behind the wheel.<P>Best!!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B><BR> He tried to get the tires to spin, they wouldnt even spin the other night when it rained.  Maybe something is wrong with it.  I noticed that the boost guage reads about 13 psi maxed out, but everywhere ive read it says stock it puts out 9 psi.  We looked every where under the hood, and cant find a boost controller, so maybe the guage is off.  <BR>And from what ive read about the later models, is stock they pull a 14.7 at about 95 mph.  And as for 60 foots I think a 2.02 is really good for a car that weighs 4000 lbs, seings how my firebird ran 2.28 60's but manages mid 14's at 99-100 mph.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
